      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Hyper-loading Vitamin C at 7000mg daily is a bold strategy, and while it may seem like a potent way to cleanse your system, it's essential to consider the potential risks. High doses of Vitamin C can lead to gastrointestinal distress, kidney stones, and other complications. A more balanced approach, with gradual increases and monitoring, is advisable. Always consult a healthcare professional before making significant changes to your supplement regimen.",
