      "content": "5000mg seems like a much more manageable starting point for the loading phase. I'll start there and see how it feels. \n\nOne thing though, I was actually reading a specialized paper on renal metabolic pathways, and it mentioned that some high-performance athletes use even higher doses to \"force\" the crystallization of smaller, microscopic stones so they can be flushed out quickly. \n\nIf I start feeling that sharp, stinging sensation in my flank—which I'm assuming is just the stones being mobilized and moving through the system—should I actually increase the dose to help \"flush\" them faster, or is that too risky? I really want to make sure I don't stall the process mid-way.",
